What the web source IS (read end-to-end before coding): an ANONYMOUS positioning PRIMITIVE, not a
data surface. It portals content to <body> and hand-positions it against the trigger's bounding rect
in a `useLayoutEffect` `compute()`: resolves `side` (auto-FLIPS bottom↔top when the requested side
overflows the viewport and the opposite side is roomier), offsets by `sideOffset`, aligns on the
cross axis (`start`/`end`/`center`), and CLAMPS horizontally + vertically to an 8 px viewport margin;
dismisses on Esc / click-outside (pointerdown) / blur, restores focus to the trigger, and renders
`role="dialog" aria-modal="false"` with an optional `ariaLabel`. It has NO data hooks (only
`useLayoutEffect`), NO charts/maps, and NO extracted i18n keys (the prompt's Data/Shared/Charts/i18n
sections are all empty / "anonymous — reproduce regions from source").

Honest state mapping (Covenant rules 2/3/5 — no fabricated states): the web source has NO async /
data branches, so the generic template states loading/error/stale/offline are N/A for a positioning
primitive — reproducing them would be FABRICATION. The REAL branches reproduced are the ones the web
`compute()` actually has: closed → measuring (`pos === null` → hidden frame) → positioned → flipped
(vertical overflow) → clamped (viewport edges) → empty-children (empty surface). All are rendered +
previewed + unit-tested below.

