Parity surface map (web -> native):
  open / onClose                       -> PopoverModel.isPresented + setPresented/present/dismiss (onClose seam)
  anchorRef.getBoundingClientRect()    -> PopoverModel.updateAnchor(_:) (container coords)
  content.getBoundingClientRect()      -> PopoverContentSizeKey preference -> PopoverModel.updateContent(_:)
  window.innerWidth/innerHeight        -> GeometryReader bounds -> PopoverModel.updateViewport(_:)
  useLayoutEffect compute() (flip)     -> PopoverGeometry.resolveSide(_:contentHeight:spaceAbove:spaceBelow:)
  compute() top/left + clamp           -> PopoverGeometry.place(anchor:content:viewport:side:align:sideOffset:margin:)
  side bottom/top  (PopoverSide)       -> PopoverSide + Edge mapping (native arrowEdge) / resolved place()
  align start/end/center (PopoverAlign)-> PopoverAlign + UnitPoint attachment / alignedLeft()
  margin = 8 / sideOffset = 6          -> PopoverGeometry.margin / .defaultSideOffset
  pos === null (hidden while sizing)   -> PopoverModel.isMeasuring -> surface opacity 0 + allowsHitTesting(false)
  Esc / click-outside / blur close     -> native `.popover` dismiss  +  PopoverContainer backdrop tap / .escape / onExitCommand(macOS)
  focus restore to trigger             -> native `.popover` focus return  +  @AccessibilityFocusState (container)
  role="dialog" / aria-modal="false"   -> accessibilityElement(children:.contain) + region label (non-trapping; web is intentionally NOT a focus trap)
  ariaLabel                            -> PopoverAccessibility.regionLabel(custom:) (else localized default)
  rounded-lg border glass-border bg surface-1 text-primary shadow-xl -> PopoverSurface chrome (TSRadius/Color.TS/shadow); forced-colors arm via dynamic tokens
  @/components/ui tokens               -> Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSAnimation (P1/S9)
  (anonymous — no useTranslation)      -> PopoverStrings (P1/S10, table "Popover", a11y fallbacks only)

Native translation rationale (Covenant rule 5 — not a shortcut): Apple platforms ship a native
`.popover` that already gives the web semantics CORRECTLY per HIG (auto-flip, viewport clamp, Esc /
click-outside dismiss, focus restore, non-modal). `popoverSurface` uses it for the common "attach to
a trigger" case and forces `.presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover)` so iPhone shows a popover (web
is always a popover, never a sheet). The web source's EXPLICIT hand-positioning math is reproduced
1:1 in `PopoverGeometry` and CONSUMED at runtime by `PopoverContainer` (the inline, bounded analogue
of the web `position:fixed` portal: flip + align + clamp + hidden measuring frame), so the engine is
genuine, used, and fully unit-tested — not decorative.

States rendered (no hidden surfaces): closed, measuring (hidden frame), positioned, flipped (top),
  clamped (viewport edges), empty-children (PopoverEmptyContent). Previews: surface populated/empty
  (light+dark), native-popover trigger, gallery bottom/start · flip-to-top · center · end(+Dynamic Type).
Telemetry: `view.opened` emitted once per open with slug "Popover" (P1/S11) — covered by test.
Accessibility: VoiceOver region label on the surface, `.escape` action + macOS Esc, Dynamic Type
  (system fonts / tokens), Reduce Motion honored via TSAnimation; trigger uses the system popover a11y.

